  {
   "text": "Built and verified. Here's what's between the UFO portal (col 10) and the cube portal (col 53):\n\n- **Spikes:** a 5-tall column at col 17 that the flight has to clear, 3-tall columns at 24, 33, 37, and 2-tall ones at 14 and 41.\n- **Yellow orb** at col 21, row 4 \u2014 head height, sitting right on the flight line, so it gets tapped mid-hop.\n- **Yellow pad** at col 26 on top of a 5-tall block platform (cols 25\u201328): the UFO lands on the platform, the pad kicks it up 16 units. In open air a ground pad is never touched, which is why it's raised.\n- Then open runway to the cube portal at col 53.\n\n`verify_section` reports it **possible** \u2014 6 presses, worst timing window 92 ms, and the exit state is `cube`, so it hands back to the cube cleanly. I also replayed the route in the simulator to confirm the orb (extra vy at x\u2248637) and the pad (16-unit impulse at x\u2248770) actually fire rather than just sitting there.\n\nTwo things I had to fix along the way: the UFO was sailing straight over the cube portal at col 46, so the portal moved out to col 53 to give it room to drop; and the first layout had the orb and pad off the flight path entirely.\n\nNot playtested in the real editor \u2014 say the word and I'll run `playtest_verify` on it. The bpm is still unset in the plan, so if you want the presses on the beat, tell me the bpm and I'll sync it.",
